.TH CONFIG 1 "September 2026" "ProwseTk" "Prowse-TUI Help"
.SH NAME
config \- ProwseTUI.toml settings editor
.SH FILE
$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/prowse/ProwseTUI.toml
.PP
When XDG_CONFIG_HOME is unset, empty, or relative, use
$HOME/.config/prowse/ProwseTUI.toml. Opening config does not create a file.
.SH EDITOR
:config opens a selectable page. Move with j/k or arrows and press Enter
on a row to prepare an edit command. Enter again confirms that command.
Edits are staged. Select Save changes or run :config save to write the file.
Esc returns to the browser and keeps staged changes until exit.
:config reload discards staged changes and reads the saved settings.
Saved keybindings apply immediately. Extension changes take effect next launch.
.SH COMMANDS
.nf
:config bind down J
:config add-lua extensions/my automation.lua
:config add-plugin plugins/my_plugin.so
:config remove-lua 1
:config remove-plugin 1
:config save
:config reload
.fi
.SH KEYS
Actions: down, up, back, activate, page_down, page_up, home, end, close,
search, next_match, previous_match, help, config.
Keys: a single printable ASCII character, Space, Tab, or F1 through F12.
Duplicate keys are rejected. To swap two keys, use an unused key temporarily.
The colon, Esc, Enter, arrow keys, PageUp, PageDown, Home, End and Ctrl-C
remain available as fixed controls. Rebindings affect normal mode only.
.SH TOML EXAMPLE
.nf
lua_extensions = ["extensions/example.lua"]
native_plugins = ["plugins/example.so"]

[keys]
down = "J"
up = "K"
help = "F1"
config = "F2"
.fi
.SH VALIDATION
Unknown fields, invalid types, duplicate keys and invalid paths are rejected.
Saving replaces the file atomically with mode 0600. The editor rewrites
formatting and comments; only the documented schema is accepted.
No cookies, form values or session data are stored in this file.
.SH SEE ALSO
.MR extensions 1
.MR overview 1
